US-075 is implemented, and every listed gate passes on Windows and Linux. The tests cover the generator and the fixture provenance table. The `linux-asan` and `linux-gcc` jobs were not run, and `engine_bench` acceptance still reports `missing` for the four scenes.

**What was built**
- **Generator (`tools/benchmark/src/workload.cpp`)**: builds each benchmark scene from its seed and the integer counts in `benchmarks/manifest.json`. It produces unique meshes, instance descriptors, animated characters with clips, lights and suns, particle emitters, physics bodies, constraints, characters, audio emitters, and a 9×9 tile terrain window. All of it is integer-only, so the digests are the same on every compiler.
- **`engine_workload` CLI**: `--write` produces the expected file and `--check` regenerates and compares it, printing any differing component.
- **Expected file (`benchmarks/workload_expected.json`)**: pins each scene's counts and one SHA-256 per component.
- **Fixture provenance (`tests/fixtures/PROVENANCE.md`)**: lists all 39 fixtures with SHA-256, source, and license. A unit test fails on any missing, extra, or changed file.
- **Tests**: 14 new unit cases (`bench_workload_tests.cpp`, `fixture_provenance_tests.cpp`). `engine_tests --suite unit` now reports 1016 cases.
- **Docs**: `docs/benchmarks.md` has a workloads section, fixture provenance, and reproduction steps. `.ralph-tui/progress.md` has the US-075 entry.

**Gates**
- Linux: ValidateVendor, `linux-dev` configure, `linux-debug` build (0 warnings), `ctest --preset linux-unit` (30 of 30), and `engine_workload --check` all pass.
- Windows (MSVC /W4 /WX): ValidateVendor, `win-dev`, `win-debug` build (0 warnings), `ctest --preset win-unit` (29 of 29), and `engine_workload --check` all pass.
- The expected file generated on Linux matches the MSVC output exactly.

**Verification of the fixtures**
- I ran the audio commands from `tests/fixtures/audio/README.md` in a scratch directory. The WAV files match byte for byte. The Ogg files decode to identical PCM, but 24 bytes differ (stream serial and page checksums), so the Ogg bytes are not reproducible.
- The model and texture generators reproduce their files byte for byte. The one JPEG (`gradient_9x7.jpg`) comes from a Windows-only script and is not regenerated here.

**Choices you may want to change**
- **No new file-format fixtures.** I read "include required file-format fixtures" as "document and verify the existing ones". Existing fixtures already cover glTF/GLB, FBX, OBJ, PNG, JPEG, WAV, and Ogg. If you want new formats added, say which.
- **No license chosen.** The repo has no `LICENSE` file, so the provenance table says "project-authored" and leaves the license open. This needs your decision.
- **Generator scope.** Terrain is heights only, and the four terrain layers are not generated. The route, cell crossings, and teleport case are left to US-076 to US-078. The `instances_within_draw_distance` checkpoint (957 of 20000 for `render_stress`) is not the resident count the route will define.
- **Scene parameters not in the table.** A 64-mesh library is used for scenes whose table names no meshes, and the world seed is fixed. Both are part of the digests, and the docs say so.

